{"ok": false, "issues": ["The requirement says the optional fee in lieu of a deposit is 'capped at 1 month's rent in total with any deposit.' The source caps only the total fee or recurring payments at 1 month's rent, and the tenant may choose a full deposit instead of the fee. Nothing in the source supports combining the fee with a deposit under one cap.", "The requirement is far longer than the 1-2 plain sentences the format calls for. It has been condensed with the substance kept."], "fix": {"requirement": "A security deposit may not exceed the first month's rent. It must be held in a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account, with a bank receipt to the tenant within 30 days and a statement of the premises' condition. Interest of 5% per year (or the lesser bank rate) is owed if the deposit is held a year or longer. The deposit must be returned within 30 days after the tenancy ends, less only unpaid rent or water charges, conforming tax-escalation amounts, or damage beyond reasonable wear and tear documented by a sworn itemized list. Since Aug 1, 2025, the Executive Office of Housing and Livable Communities may by regulation authorize an optional, tenant-elective fee in lieu of a deposit, with total fee payments capped at 1 month's rent."}}
